 `useWalkthroughStore.ts` keys entries, model and language choices, active requests, and progress pollers by runtime plus the full walkthrough target. Working-tree and branch targets need only their Git source. A pull-request target also carries the immutable `SourceControlReadContext` that discovered it, so equal PR numbers under different accounts, repositories, bindings, or provider instances cannot share client state. The client sends that context on every PR walkthrough operation and rejects successful read or generation responses unless they echo the exact authority tuple. Runtime reset aborts active requests, stops pollers, and clears pending entry-point targets before the new endpoint can reuse them.
 
+## Quota refresh extensions
+
+`useQuotaStore.fetchProviderQuota` deduplicates per-provider work and invokes the optional provider refresh hook from `lib/quota/providers` alongside the ordinary quota read. Hook settlement never blocks the ordinary read's deadline, completion, loading cleanup or deduplication release. Hook failure does not suppress that read. The request abort signal fences runtime reset and `invalidateProvider(id)`; provider invalidation clears only that provider's result and error, preserving unrelated providers and display settings. Hook registration returns identity-safe cleanup.
+
+A surface joins the shared three-minute refresh only while it is open by passing its open state as `useQuotaAutoRefresh`'s `visible` argument. Product-specific refresh mechanics belong in the product package, not this store.
+
 ## Ownership Rules
 
 These rules are important. Breaking them tends to reintroduce idle CPU churn, stale UI, or rerender fanout.
